police search an area of westland in  parkland on the final day of what's  become the bloodiest year for teen  killings in the capital  two teenage boys aged 15 and 16 were  pronounced dead within minutes of each  other last night in separate incidents  the mets say it's too early to tell if  the incidents are linked  but the double tragedy brings the total  number of teenage killings in london to  30 this calendar year posing serious  questions for the met and the mayor of  london  the problem is even though there are  fewer young people being stabbed even  though there are fewer young people  going to hospital with these injuries we  have a large number who losing their  lives the ferocity of some of these  stabbings the ferociousness  of some of these attacks is what causes  me concern and that's why we're going to  continue to support our police  officers continue to hunt for clues  searching here in usd in west london  where the 16 year old boy was killed and  more than 20 miles away in crowden where  just moments before a 15 year old also  lost their life and these aren't just  numbers these are young lives and their  loss has a traumatizing impact on  communities  i have children the same age  children that knew this young person  and for me  you know i'm nearly 50 and i have never  been  to a funeral of somebody i went to  school with  and here is my child  in six months in her school  death of two  of her classmates  the police say they continued to work  with local communities to get knives off  the streets but shortly after speaking  to sky news a church pastor says she was  contacted by a worried mother pleading  for her help i've had a phone call from  a mother  who is going through her washing basket  and has come across a knife  phone call pass the barrel please can  you come and pick this up come and  collect it  this is a mother who is in tears  and her thinking is is this going to  stop my child being killed or my child  killing somebody else  2021 closes as it began  with police promising to bring justice  to victims families and take weapons off  the streets  nevertheless we enter 2022 with a new  grim record  one that no one asked to be set  shimane freeman powell sky news
 

